# OpticWise Brand & Content Rule

Whenever the user asks for content to be created, written, drafted, edited, repositioned, or proofed — blog posts, LinkedIn posts/articles, web copy, sales collateral, emails, talk tracks, decks, case studies, image prompts, or anything else that represents OpticWise externally OR internally — you MUST follow the OpticWise brand canon.

**Read the connected guidelines before writing a single word:**

@opticwise-brand-guidelines.md

The connected file is the synthesized canon (SB7 BrandScript, Sales Playbook, PPP 5C™ plan, Asset Manager Mindset Overlay, Bill/Drew voice canons, Content Engine rules, approved Wins & Nightmares, NOI benchmarks, banned words, trademark rules). It is non-negotiable and overrides anything in this codebase that contradicts it.

**Source canon lives in:**
`/Users/billdouglas/My Drive/AA DOWNLOADS - WD rev 2025-Apr/Claude CoWork Projects/OpticWise Content Engine/`

If the user asks a content question and the connected guidelines do not cover it, ask before improvising — never invent client names, numbers, quotes, or proof points.

## Hard rules (do not violate, ever)

- Always say **"data & digital infrastructure"** — never "infrastructure" alone.
- Never frame OpticWise as **"PropTech."**
- Use **"owner"** (not "REIT"), **"review"** (not "audit" for the OW engagement), and **"operations / utilities optimization"** (never "ESG").
- Every trademark, every mention: **Peak Property Performance®, PPP 5C™, BoT®, Building of Things®, ElasticISP®, SIC®, 5S®, Property Brain™, Portfolio Brain™**.
- Banned words: *leverage, synergy, ecosystem, holistic, seamless, cutting-edge, ESG, PropTech*.
- Default audience lens is the **asset manager** (not property manager / IT). Property managers, IT, and engineers are read-through stakeholders, not the buyer.
- Never invent client names, metrics, quotes, case studies, or outcomes. Use only approved Wins & Nightmares; otherwise frame as *"a common pattern we see…"* with no numbers.
- Use the reframing line at least once per blog/article: **"If you don't own your data & digital infrastructure, your vendors do."**
- Default closer when the close calls for it: **"Own your data & digital infrastructure. Operate with strategic foresight. Build for the long game."**

